    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.hues\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nIt might be nice idea, to add a configuration option to enable some italic highltight groups in mini.hues. Probably not as a default, but having some things like Comments or such in optional italic fonts can look nice. I'm currently doing this manually with overwriting highlight groups, but it think this could be a popular option.\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a78c7831-aa31-478d-ae7b-74aac9c53600)\r\n\r\nEdit: Just adding the code from the screenshot if someone comes across this and wants to copy it:\r\n```\r\nlocal function mod_hl(hl_name, opts)\r\n    local is_ok, hl_def = pcall(vim.api.nvim_get_hl_by_name, hl_name, true)\r\n    if is_ok then\r\n        for k, v in pairs(opts) do hl_def[k] = v end\r\n        vim.api.nvim_set_hl(0, hl_name, hl_def)\r\n    end\r\nend\r\n\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"VimEnter\", \"ColorScheme\" }, {\r\n    group = vim.api.nvim_create_augroup('Color', {}),\r\n    pattern = \"*\",\r\n    callback = function()\r\n        mod_hl(\"Comment\", { italic = true })\r\n        mod_hl(\"@comment\", { italic = true })\r\n        mod_hl(\"MiniTablineVisible\", { italic = true })\r\n        mod_hl(\"MiniTablineCurrent\", { italic = true })\r\n    end\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\n",
