            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nI personally don't really like italic font variants, so it won't be part of config, sorry. Manually making target highlight groups (which users want) to be italic is the suggested approach here. This can be achieved by `vim.cmd.highlight('Comment gui=italic')`, for example. Or with the approach shown in screenshot, which is more versatile indeed.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
